## 🎮 Overview

In **Cook**, you have **3 minutes (180 seconds)** to fulfill as many customer orders as possible. Customers line up along 4 service windows on the kitchen wall, demanding various combinations of cooked meat patties, sliced vegetables, and cheese. Manage your time wisely: retrieve raw ingredients from the refrigerator, sear meats on the dual-slot stove, slice veggies at the prep counter, and deliver completed plates before order timers tick down.

---

## 🔁 Gameplay Loop

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Start Game: 3 Min Timer] --> B[Check Customer Windows 1-4]
    B --> C[Fetch Ingredients from Refrigerator]
    C --> D{Needs Preparation?}
    D -- Meat --> E[Cook on Stove: 6.0s]
    D -- Vegetables --> F[Slice at Prep Table: 2.0s]
    D -- Cheese --> G[Ready to Serve]
    E --> G
    F --> G
    G --> H[Place on Customer Window Plate]
    H --> I{All Items Delivered?}
    I -- No --> B
    I -- Yes --> J[Order Completed: Points Tallied!]
    J --> K[5s Respawn Delay -> New Customer]

Start: The game opens with a Controls & Instructions window. Click Begin Game (or press Space/Enter) to start the 3-minute session.
Orders: 4 customer windows immediately open with randomized recipe orders.
Prep: Pick up ingredients from the refrigerator, cook raw meat on the stove, and chop vegetables at the prep counter.
Serve: Deliver items to the counter plate at the matching customer window.
Score: Once all required ingredients are placed on the plate, the order is fulfilled, points are awarded with floating visual feedback, and a new customer arrives after 5 seconds.
Game Over: When the 3-minute countdown reaches zero, the game ends, displaying your final score, high score, and a New High Score! banner if you set a record.
⌨ Controls
Action	Primary Key	Alternate Input
Move Up / Forward	W	▲ Up Arrow
Move Down / Backward	S	▼ Down Arrow
Move Left	A	◄ Left Arrow
Move Right	D	► Right Arrow
Interact / Pick Up / Place	E	Left Mouse Click
Refrigerator: Quick Meat	1	Refrigerator UI Button
Refrigerator: Quick Cheese	2	Refrigerator UI Button
Refrigerator: Quick Vegetables	3	Refrigerator UI Button
Pause / Resume Game	P	Esc / On-screen Pause Button
Restart Game	R	Restart Button (Pause / Game Over)
Begin Game / Confirm	Space	Enter / UI Button
⚠️ Important Notes
IMPORTANT

To use the Refrigerator, you need to rotate the character correctly: The player interaction system utilizes forward directional targeting (Physics.SphereCastNonAlloc). Make sure your character is turned to directly face the front of the Refrigerator to bring up the interaction prompt and retrieve ingredients.

Tip: Walk directly toward the refrigerator counter before pressing E or 1/2/3.

Single-Item Capacity: The chef can hold one item at a time in hand. To switch items, place your current item on a valid station/plate or discard it in the Trash.
Overcooked Food: Do not leave cooked meat patties on the stove for too long after they finish searing, or they will burn into Overcooked food that customers will reject!
Trash Station: Any raw, burnt, or unwanted ingredient can be permanently discarded in the Trash can next to the counter.
🍽 Kitchen Stations & Recipes
1. 🧊 Refrigerator
Function: Infinite pantry providing raw cooking staples.
Available Items:
🥩 Raw Meat (Requires cooking on the stove)
🧀 Cheese (Ready to serve immediately)
🥦 Raw Vegetables (Requires chopping on the table)
Shortcuts: Press 1 for Meat, 2 for Cheese, or 3 for Veggies when facing the unit.
2. 🔥 Dual-Slot Stove
Function: Searing meat patties.
Capacity: 2 independent cooking slots.
Cook Duration: 6.0 seconds per patty.
Features: Autonomous cooking progress bars, dual-card WorldSpace display, and real-time visual transformation from raw red meat to cooked brown patties.
3. 🔪 Prep Table / Chopping Board
Function: Slicing raw vegetables.
Capacity: 1 item at a time.
Chop Duration: 2.0 seconds.
Features: Live circular/countdown progress gauge, transforming whole veggies into diced culinary slices.
4. 🗑 Trash Can
Function: Cleans up kitchen messes.
Behavior: Instantly destroys any held item (raw ingredients, chopped items, cooked patties, or burnt food).
5. 🪟 Customer Windows (Windows 1 - 4)
Function: Order pickup & delivery counter.
Capacity: 4 simultaneous customer windows.
Features:
Live WorldSpace order ticket floating above each counter.
Physical Vector Checkboxes: Automatically displays a green box with a crisp white tick mark ✔ both when you hold the ingredient in hand ([E]) and when it has been placed on the counter plate (COLLECTED).
True 3D plate holder ensuring delivered items maintain their natural proportions without squishing.
5.0-second respawn timer between completed orders.
🎯 Customer Orders & Scoring
Ingredient Score Values
Ingredient	Preparation Required	Base Score
Cooked Patty	Sear on Stove (6.0s)	+30 Points
Sliced Vegetables	Chop on Table (2.0s)	+20 Points
Cheese	None (Ready to Serve)	+10 Points
Dynamic Scoring Formula
The final score for each fulfilled order is determined dynamically by the formula: 
Order Score
=
∑
(
Base Values of Required Ingredients
)
−
⌊
Elapsed Seconds
⌋
Order Score=∑(Base Values of Required Ingredients)−⌊Elapsed Seconds⌋

Speed Bonus: Delivering orders quickly rewards maximum points.
Floating Visual Feedback: Upon completion, a floating score indicator (+Pts) rises and fades smoothly above the window.
Persistent High Scores: Scores are saved locally via PlayerPrefs and compared against all-time records.
