Floating Visual Feedback: Upon completion, a floating score indicator (+Pts) rises and fades smoothly above the window.
Persistent High Scores: Scores are saved locally via PlayerPrefs and compared against all-time records.

🖥 UI & Menus
Main Menu: Clean start screen with Play Game and Quit Game options, mouse cursor integration, and keyboard shortcuts.
Controls & How to Play Dialog: Appears at match launch while gameplay is paused, detailing keybindings and station workflows.

In-Game HUD:
Real-time 3:00 countdown timer.
Persistent Current Score and High Score display.
Quick Pause and Quit buttons.
Pause Menu: Allows players to Resume, Restart, return to Main Menu, or Quit.
Game Over Screen: Automatically triggers when the 3-minute timer hits zero. Shows final points, high score comparison, and a glowing gold "New High Score!" banner for record-breaking runs.


🏗 Code Architecture
The project is structured with modularity, clean separation of concerns, and zero per-frame garbage collection allocations:



Assets/
├── Editor/                         # Custom Unity Editor inspectors & tools
│   ├── OrderEditorWindow.cs        # Live Editor window monitoring all 4 customer orders
│   ├── SetupHierarchyPanels.cs     # Editor utility creating/verifying all in-game UI panels
│   └── ...
├── Scenes/
│   ├── MainMenu.unity              # Start menu scene
│   └── GameScene.unity              # Core gameplay kitchen scene
└── Scripts/
    ├── GameManager.cs              # Game state machine, 3-minute timer & scorekeeper
    ├── GameState.cs                # Enum: WaitingToStart, Playing, Paused, GameOver
    ├── PlayerController.cs         # Smooth 3D physics-based character movement
    ├── PlayerInteractor.cs         # Non-alloc directional interaction & carry system
    ├── Kitchen/
    │   ├── IngredientType.cs       # Enum: Meat, CookedPatty, Veggies, SlicedVeggies, Cheese, Overcooked
    │   ├── KitchenObject.cs        # 3D interactive food item entity
    │   └── IngredientDatabase.cs   # Mesh & material factory for culinary assets
    ├── Orders/
    │   ├── Order.cs                # Order data model, fulfillment logic & score calculator
    │   └── OrderManager.cs         # Order distributor & window manager
    └── Stations/
        ├── BaseStation.cs          # Abstract base class for all kitchen counters
        ├── CustomerWindowStation.cs# Customer window, plates, UI tickets & vector checkboxes
        ├── RefrigeratorStation.cs  # Fridge counter logic & shortcut dispatcher
        ├── StoveStation.cs         # Dual-slot autonomous cooking station
        ├── TableStation.cs         # Cutting board timer & visual transformer
        └── TrashStation.cs         # Disposal counter


Key Engineering Highlights:
Zero-Allocation Physics: Interaction detection uses pre-allocated buffers (Physics.SphereCastNonAlloc, Physics.OverlapSphereNonAlloc).
Vector Checkbox Rendering: Checkmark ticks are constructed from procedural UI vector primitives—eliminating missing-glyph square boxes (□) inherent to standard TextMeshPro font packages.
Event-Driven UI: GameManager communicates state, timer, and score changes through C# Action delegates, decoupling gameplay logic from presentation.

🚀 Getting Started
Prerequisites
Unity Version: Unity 6 (6000.0.44f1 or later recommended).
Render Pipeline: Universal Render Pipeline (URP).
Target OS: Windows 10 / 11 (64-bit).
